          "expr": "sum by (node) (kube_pod_container_resource_requests{resource=\"memory\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{node}}: requested",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum by (node) (kube_node_status_allocatable{resource=\"memory\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{node}}: allocatable",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Memory requested vs allocatable, per node",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "description": "What the scheduler has promised on each node against what it can promise. A node whose requests reach allocatable cannot take another pod, and its new pods sit Pending. On k3d and kind every node advertises the whole machine's memory as allocatable, so the scheduler can promise several times the memory that exists; watch the sum of requests against the machine, not each node."
